GL chain, added 2026-10-23 (docs/analysis/mesa-rebase-2026-10.md 9). These six are not prebuilts and
are deliberately not in this directory: libOSMesa.8.dylib, libredwoodair.dylib and air_run are what
tools/mk-mesa.sh writes to xnu-deps/build/mesa/out, and the GL branch of userland/build.sh copies
them to userland/obj and links libredwood-gl.dylib, gl_test and u2f_test against the same out/ tree,
so all six move together with the out/built-from and out/built-from-air stamps and no stamp mismatch
can leave this table standing. The paths are the ones the last `GL=1 ./build.sh` left them at in the
merged tree (common/setup.sh), and root/lib and root/bin -- what the apfs images are packed from --
hold byte-identical copies of the same names. build.sh checks nothing here; to recheck from the
merged tree root: (cd hackios-xnu-kernel && sha256sum -c <(grep -E '^[0-9a-f]{64}  userland/obj/' prebuilt/userland/SHA256SUMS)),
where a mismatch means the tree has been built from different sources than the lines below.

